# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. The grace period is what
# stops a late write the tombstone beats from resurrecting the key at s; without it
# s holds the old value and r holds the delete.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceReapInsideGrace
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a tombstone is reaped while a write it beats is still on its way, which then resurrects the key
PERTURBS: Reap

--- FIND
    /\ \A i \in (cursor[<<r, s>>] + 1)..Len(wal[r]) : wal[r][i].h > reg[s].h
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no grace period.
    /\ TRUE
--- END
